<attribute name="version" nodeId="646d9130"></attribute>
<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="ed9aab30">&lt;p&gt;
    Dependency registers may contain the following attributes:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Unique Reference – used to identify dependency
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Description – used to briefly describe the dependency
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Enabling Program or Project – who must deliver the task, milestone, etc (sometimes known as the ‘giver’).
        Applicable for larger scale programs.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Dependent Program or Project – who needs the task, milestone to be delivered (sometimes known as the ‘receiver’).
        Applicable for larger scale programs.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Dependent Activity, Task, or Milestone – details of milestone / task that needs the delivery
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Delivery Date – date dependency must be delivered by to not cause a delay in dependent project
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Probability – probability that dependency will not be met in required timeline
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Date Raised – date dependency was raised
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;p&gt;
            Representation Options:
        &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Dependency registers may show dependencies using a map, so teams can see dependencies across projects / work streams.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Impact – impact of dependency not being delivered in required timeline
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Status – open, closed, etc.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Owner – who owns the dependency
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="32e6524a"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="2d497068"></attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="9374c7f2"></attribute>
<attribute name="purpose" nodeId="cf1a22eb">&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        To assist with critical path planning
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        To identify constraints on the prioritization and scheduling of work
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        To help mitigate variances to a plan
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        To provide a simple view for tracking key dependencies
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
